A banner written in SSL comment style (`/*` closed by `;`, not `*/`) above
a SQL-mode header. The header split masks it like a terminated banner, so
the body classifies on its own content and stays SQL
(feature.diagnostics_pipeline A31). The style guide's
datasource_sql_comment_syntax rule calls this form wrong in a SQL data
source but is reviewer-enforced, so no diagnostic is expected for it.
-- input.ds --
/* Data source: pallet movements by dock;
:DSN := DATABASE;
:PARAMETERS nDock := 1;

select m.move_id, m.pallet_no
from pallet_move m
where m.dock_no = @nDock
-- format --
/* Data source: pallet movements by dock;
:DSN := DATABASE;
:PARAMETERS nDock := 1;

select m.move_id, m.pallet_no
from pallet_move m
where m.dock_no = @nDock
